          %h3#introduction Introduction
          %ul
            %li#RhoEtAl16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mannque+Rho"} Mannque Rho
              et al.,
              %em Introduction
          %blockquote
            %p
              One can make
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral perturbation theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              consistent with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              by suitably matching the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective theory
              to those of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              at a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale"} scale
              near
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
              in an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang–Mills
              type form. We will see in Part III that such a structure arises,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top-down+model+building"} top-down
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              model comes out to describe — unexpectedly well — low-energy properties of both
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+QCD"} lattice QCD
              simulations.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              One of the most noticeable results of this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} holographic model
              is the first derivation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} vector dominance
              (VD) that holds both for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
              and for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jun+John+Sakurai"} Sakurai's
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} vector dominance
              — with the lowest
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rho+meson"} ρ
              and ω — which held very well for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pionic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/form+factors"} form factors
              at low momentum transfers famously failed for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleon"} nucleon
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/form+factors"} form factors
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} holographic model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} VD
              comes out automatically for both the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleon"} nucleon
              provided that the infinite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} KK-
              = succeed "tower" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} VD
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
              with the infinite tower is not surprising given the successful Sakurai VD, that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson+dominance"} VD
              holds also for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nucleons"} nucleons
              is highly nontrivial.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              It turns out to be a consequence of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} holographic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheshire+cat+principle"} Cheshire Cat phenomenon
          %h3#hadrons_and_nuclear_matter Hadrons and Nuclear Matter
          %p
