          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} models
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+nuclei"} atomic nuclei
            all the way up to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/carbon"} carbon
          %ul
            %li#BattyeMantonSutcliffe10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+A.+Battye"}> Richard A. Battye
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicholas+Manton"} Nicholas Manton
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Sutcliffe"} Paul Sutcliffe
              = succeed "," do
                %em Skyrmions and Nuclei
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814280709_0001"} doi:10.1142/9789814280709_0001
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong Chapter 2
          %ul
            %li#Holzwarth05
              Gottfried Holzwarth,
              %em Electromagnetic Form Factors of the Nucleon in Chiral Soliton Models
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0511194"}> arXiv:hep-ph/0511194
              ), Chapter 2 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Multifaceted+Skyrmion"} The Multifaceted Skyrmion
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong Chapter 3
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Diakonov"}> Dmitri Diakonov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Petrov"} Victor Petrov
              %em Exotic baryon resonances in the Skyrme model
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0812.1212"}> arXiv:0812.1212
              ,
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814704410_0004"} doi:10.1142/9789814704410_0004
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Multifaceted+Skyrmion"} The Multifaceted Skyrmion
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
          %blockquote
            %p
              It is astounding that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tony+Skyrme"} Skyrme
              had suggested
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} his model
              as early as in 1961 before it has been generally accepted that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
              are (pseudo)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goldstone+bosons"} Goldstone bosons
              associated with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} spontaneous breaking
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry"} chiral symmetry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} Quantum Chromodynamics (QCD)
              has been put forward as the microscopic theory of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+nuclear+force"} strong interactions
            %p
              The revival of the Skyrme idea in 1983 is
              %a{:href => "Skyrmion#Witten83"} due to Witten
              who explained the
              %em raison d’ˆetre
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} Skyrme model
              from the viewpoint of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral limit
              when the light
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark"} quark
              masses
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi u
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_u
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi m
                        %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_d
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi m
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_s
              tend to zero, such that the octet of the pseudoscalar mesons
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} π
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kaon"} K
              , η become nearly massless (pseudo)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goldstone+bosons"} Goldstone bosons
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
              chiral Lagrangian (EχL) for pseudoscalar mesons, understood as an infinite expansion in the derivatives of the pseudoscalar (or chiral) fields, encodes, in principle, full information about QCD. The famous two-term Skyrme Lagrangian can be understood as a low-energy truncation of this infinite series. Witten has added an important four-derivative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW-term"} Wess–Zumino term
              to the original Skyrme Lagrangian and pointed out that the overall coefficient in front of the EχL is proportional to the number of quark
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} colours
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_c
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              Soon after Witten’s work it has been realized that it is possible to bring the Skyrme model and the Skyrmion even closer to QCD and to the more customary language of constituent quarks. It has been first noticed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#DiakonovEides83"} 6
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#DharWadia84"} 7a
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#DarShankarWadia85"} 7b
              %a{:href => "#DiakonovPetrov86"} 8
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              that a simple chiral invariant Lagrangian for massive (constituent) quarks
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              interacting with the octet chiral field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_A
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo .
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 8
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A = 1, ..., 8)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mi Q
                      %mo ¯
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo ∂
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo −
                      %mi M
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %msup
                                %mi π
                                %mi A
                              %msup
                                %mi λ
                                %mi A
                              %msub
                                %mi γ
                                %mn 5
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi F
                                %mi π
                      %mo )
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{L} = \overline{Q} \left( \partial\!\!\!\!/ - M e^{ \tfrac{i \pi^A \lambda^A \gamma_5}{F_\pi}  }  \right) Q
            %p induces, via a quark loop in the external pseudoscalar fields (see Fig. 3.1), the EχL whose lowest-derivative terms coincide with the Skyrme Lagrangian, including automatically the Wess–Zumino term, with the correct coefficient!
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/DiakonovPetrovQuarkLoop.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              The condition that the winding number of the trial field is unity needs to be imposed to get a deeply bound state, that is to guarantee that the baryon number is unity.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "#DiakonovPetrovPobylitsa88"} 9
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              The Skyrmion is, thus, nothing but the
              = succeed "." do
                %strong mean chiral field binding quarks in a baryon
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/DiakonovPetrovMeanField.jpg", :width => "600"}/
          %p
            %br/
          %ul
            %li#DiakonovEides83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Diakonov"}> Dmitri Diakonov
                , Michael I. Eides,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chiral Lagrangian from a functional integral over quarks
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://jetpletters.ac.ru/ps/1483/article_22635.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/DiakonovEides83.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#DharWadia84
              %p
                A. Dhar, Spenta R. Wadia,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nambu—Jona-Lasinio Model: An Effective Lagrangian for Quantum Chromodynamics at Intermediate Length Scales
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.959"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.52.959
            %li#DarShankarWadia85
              %p
                Avinash Dhar, R. Shankar, Spenta R. Wadia,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nambu–Jona-Lasinio–type effective Lagrangian: Anomalies and nonlinear Lagrangian of low-energy, large-N QCD
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.31.3256"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.31.3256
            %li#DiakonovPetrov86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Diakonov"}> Dmitri Diakonov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Petrov"} Victor Petrov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A theory of light quarks in the instanton vacuum
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(86)90011-8"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(86)90011-8
            %li#DiakonovPetrovPobylitsa88
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Diakonov"}> Dmitri Diakonov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Petrov"} Victor Petrov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Chiral Theory of Nucleons
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/247700"} spire:247700
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(88)90443-9"} doi:10.1016/0550-3213(88)90443-9
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong Chapter 4
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
            with
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heavy+mesons"} heavy mesons
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Norberto+Scoccola"}> Norberto Scoccola
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Heavy quark skyrmions
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0905.2722"} arXiv:0905.2722
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814280709_0004"} doi:10.1142/9789814280709_0004
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Multifaceted+Skyrmion"} The Multifaceted Skyrmion
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong Chapter 5
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion+model"} Skyrmion model
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermal+QFT"} thermal QFT
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/omega-meson"} omega-meson
            = succeed "-coupling:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon+current"} baryon current
          %ul
            %li#ParkVento09
              Byung-Yoon Park, Vicente Vento,
              %em Skyrmion approach to finite density and temperature
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0906.3263"}> arXiv:0906.3263
              ,
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814280709_0005"} doi:10.1142/9789814280709_0005
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Multifaceted+Skyrmion"} The Multifaceted Skyrmion
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong Chapter 6
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+bosons"} gauge bosons
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hidden+local+symmetry"} hidden local symmetry
            and then as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} KK-modes
            of a 5-dimensional holographic
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
          %ul
            %li
              Hyun Kyu Lee,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mannque+Rho"} Mannque Rho
              %em Half-Skyrmion Hadronic Matter at High Density
              (
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814280709_0006"}> doi:10.1142/9789814280709_0006
              ), Chapter 6 in:
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mannque+Rho"} Mannque Rho
              et al.,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Multifaceted Skyrmion
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
          %h3#condensed_matter Condensed matter
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+matter+physics"} condensed matter physics
          %p (…)
          %h3#string_theory String theory
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skyrmion"} skyrmion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            appearing within the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Sakai-Sugimoto model
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+quantum+chromodynamics"} holographic quantum chromodynamics
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D5+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} D=5 super Yang-Mills theory
          %p
            %strong Chapter 15
          %ul
            %li#Sugimoto16
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeki+Sugimoto"}> Shigeki Sugimoto
              ,
              %em Skyrmions and String theory
          %p
            %strong Chapter 16
          %ul
            %li#Yi09
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Piljin+Yi"}> Piljin Yi
              ,
              %em Holographic Baryons
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0902.4515"}> arXiv:0902.4515
              ,
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.worldscientific.com/doi/abs/10.1142/9789814280709_0016"} doi:10.1142/9789814280709_0016
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mannque+Rho"} Mannque Rho
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ismail+Zahed"} Ismail Zahed
              (eds.)
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Multifaceted+Skyrmion"} The Multifaceted Skyrmion
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
          %blockquote
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              is a challenging theory. Its most interesting aspects, namely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
              and the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry+breaking"} chiral symmetry breaking
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+gauge+theory"} lattice gauge theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              below the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale"} scale
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              it has been proposed early on that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              are topological
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solitons"} solitons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmions"} Skyrmions
              = succeed "but" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              the usual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} Skyrmion
              picture of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
              has to be modified significantly in the context of full
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
              the holographic picture naturally brings a gauge principle in the bulk description of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+physics"} flavor
              dynamics in such a way that all spin one
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
              as well as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
              would enter the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Skyrmion"} skyrmionic
              = succeed "construction" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              on the equal footing.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              is similar to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+perturbation+theory"} chiral perturbation theory
              in the sense that we deal with exclusively
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+invariance"} gauge-invariant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} operators
              of the theory. The huge difference is, however, that this new approach tends to treat all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+invariance"} gauge-invariant
              objects together. Not only the light
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson"} meson
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
              like
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
              but also heavy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+mesons"} vector mesons
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
              appear together, at least in principle. In other words, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              deals with all
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+representation"} singlets
              simultaneously, giving us a lot more predictive power.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
          %blockquote
            %p
              The expectation that there exists a more intelligent theory consisting only of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+invariance"} gauge-invariant
              objects in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} large Nc limit
              is thus realized via
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              in a somewhat surprising manner that the master fields, those truly physical degrees of freedom, actually live not in four dimensional Minkowskian world but in five or higher dimensional curved geometry. This is not however completely unanticipated, and was heralded in the celebrated work by
              %a{:href => "#EguchiKawai82"} Eguchi and Kawai in early 1980’s
              which is all the more remarkable in retrospect.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              To compare against actual
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
              = succeed "the" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%27t+Hooft+coupling"} 't Hooft coupling
              and the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+compactification"} KK
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale"} scale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              to fit both the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
              decay constant
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\pi
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
              of the first
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson"} vector meson
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/masses"} masses
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constants"} coupling constants
              are fixed. This version
              = succeed "the" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WSS+model"} WSS model
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
              is extremely predictive.
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo .
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [...]
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              this
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              elevates the classic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skyrmion"} Skyrme picture
              based on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
              to a unified model involving all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+meson"} spin one mesons
              in addition to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pions"} pions
            %p
              As we saw in this note, for low momentum processes, such as soft
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitude"} processes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rho+meson"} rho meson
              exchanges, and soft elastic scattering of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/photons"} photons
              = succeed "holographic" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WSS+model"} WSS
              = succeed "model\u2019s" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
              sector works out almost as well as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson"} meson
              sector
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong Chapter 17
          %p
            On deriving the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cheshire+cat+principle"} Cheshire cat principle
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark+bag+model"} quark bag model
            from
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} AdS/QCD
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Holger+Bech+Nielsen"}> Holger Bech Nielsen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ismail+Zahed"} Ismail Zahed
              %em The Cheshire Cat Principle from Holography
              (
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814280709_0017"}> doi:10.1142/9789814280709_0017
              ,
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.0429"} arXiv:0904.0429
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Multifaceted+Skyrmion"} The Multifaceted Skyrmion
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong Chapter 18
          %p
            On deriving
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/masses"} masses
            from
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
          %ul
            %li#PomarolWulzer09
              Alex Pomarol, Andrea Wulzer,
              %em Baryon physics in a five-dimensional model of hadrons
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.2272"}> arXiv:0904.2272
              ), Chapter 18 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mannque+Rho"} Mannque Rho
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ismail+Zahed"} Ismail Zahed
              (eds.)
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Multifaceted+Skyrmion"} The Multifaceted Skyrmion
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9710"} doi:10.1142/9710
          %p (…)
